{"node_id": "real_056_batch_51_2024-Issue6.NEW_.508C_.070924_7_HY_003", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0009"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0009_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Treating a general medical problem can often restore your sense\nof taste. For example, if you have a cold or allergies, your ability\nto taste will likely improve as you feel better. You could also get\nyour taste back spontaneously. Proper oral hygiene is important\nto regaining and maintaining a well-functioning sense of taste.\nIf you're experiencing taste problems, you could also prepare\nyour food differently.", "semantic_text": "Treating a general medical problem can often restore your sense of taste. For example, if you have a cold or allergies, your ability to taste will likely improve as you feel better. You could also get your taste back spontaneously. Proper oral hygiene is important to regaining and maintaining a well-functioning sense of taste. If you're experiencing taste problems, you could also prepare your food differently.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0009_geometry", "bbox": [68, 1035, 578, 1217], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0009"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_20/hybrid/real_056_batch_51_2024-Issue6.NEW_.508C_.070924/page_0007/decisions.json"}
